<td style=" color:#000000; font-size:12pt; background-color:#FFFFFF; font-family:arial; bLabel:main; bEditID:r3st1;" tEditID="c1r1" locked="0" aEditID="c1r1" >
<![CDATA[<p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Thank you for your
interest in the Master of Science in exercise and wellness (MS EXW) program.
Students who have completed the following requirements are encouraged to apply:<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">1.&nbsp;&nbsp; Bachelor’s
degree from a regionally accredited college or university.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">2.</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">GRE scores</span></b><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;"> at or above the <b>50<sup>th</sup> percentile</b>.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">3.</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Minimum <b>GPA</b> of <b>3.0</b>.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-indent: -0.25in;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">4.</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;">&nbsp;&nbsp; </span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">Completion of the following undergraduate course
deficiencies prior to or during graduate coursework. These courses are offered
at ASU each semester (fall, spring, and summer) in order to facilitate
completion of requirements. The undergraduate course deficiencies do not count
toward the 36 credit hour graduate degree.<o:p></o:p></span></p><p class="MsoNormal" style="margin-bottom: 0.0001pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Arial, sans-serif;">&nbsp;<o:p></o:p></span></p><table class="MsoNormalTable" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="border-collapse:collapse;mso-yfti-tbllook:1184;mso-padding-alt:0in 0in 0in 0in">
